# Future-time queries, e.g. "what time will it be in 5 minutes",
# "in 2 hours what time will it be", "what time is it after ten seconds".
# {number:offset} anchors the number for the engine; the handler re-parses the whole
# utterance to extract the exact duration, so any number/unit phrasing is caught.
in {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [from now] what time will it (be|become|show) [in {location}]
what time (is it|will it be|will it become|will it show) (in|after) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [from now] [in {location}]
what time (is it|will it be|will it become|will it show) if i (wait|spend) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [in {location}]
what time (is it|will it be) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [from now] [in {location}]
what will the clock say (in|after|if i wait) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [in {location}]
when (is it|will it be) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [from now] [in {location}]
when will it be if i (wait|spend) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [in {location}]
when time will it (be|become|show) (in|after|if i wait) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [in {location}]
what time is it going to be (in|after) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] [from now] [in {location}]
what time will it be in {location} (in|after) {number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s]
{number:offset} (hour|minute|second)[s] from now what time will it be [in {location}]
what time will it be in an hour
what time will it be in a couple of hours
what time will it be in a quarter of an hour
what time will it be an hour from now
what will the time be in an hour
what time will it be in {location} in {number:offset} (hour|minute)[s]
what time will it be {number:offset} (hour|minute)[s] from now in {location}
tell me the time it will be {number:offset} hours later
what will my clock show {number:offset} minutes later
add {number:offset} hours to the current time
work out the time {number:offset} hours ahead of now
which time will the clock show after {number:offset} minutes have passed
